Since gui-gate 0.9.7 every gui-gate release archive also carries the unmodified
official Cua Driver release build of the version pinned in scripts/cua-driver.lock
(downloaded from trycua/cua's GitHub release at gui-gate's release time and
verified against that release's SHA256SUMS and Sigstore bundle). It is
redistributed under its MIT License, whose text ships next to it in the archive
(cua-driver/LICENSE). gui-gate runs it as a separate child process
(`cua-driver mcp`); gui-gate's own source does not include Cua Driver's code.
